    {
      "group": "6-Pin SOT-23-6 / TSOT-23-6 Buck Converters",
      "parts": ["TPS54302DDCR", "TPS563201DDCR", "AP62200WU-7", "AP63203WU-7"],
      "finding": "TPS54302DDCR, TPS563201DDCR, and AP62200WU-7 share the exact pinout (1=GND, 2=SW, 3=VIN, 4=FB, 5=EN, 6=BOOT/VBST/BST), whereas Diodes AP63203WU-7 uses an incompatible scrambled pinout (1=FB, 2=EN, 3=VIN, 4=GND, 5=SW, 6=BST) AND is fixed 3.3 V at 1.1 MHz. Even among the three pin-identical parts, critical traps block blind swaps: (1) EN abs max is 7 V on TPS54302 and 8 V on AP62200 (float to enable) vs 19 V with internal 1.5 MOhm pulldown on TPS563201 (float disables it!); (2) VREF differs sharply (0.596 V vs 0.768 V vs 0.800 V, causing up to +34% VOUT error); (3) VIN max is 28 V on TPS54302 vs 18 V on AP62200 and 17 V on TPS563201; (4) AP62200 recommends 330 nF Cbst for VOUT > 3 V."
    },
    {
      "group": "5-Pin SOT-23-5 High-Voltage Non-Synchronous Boost Converters",
      "parts": ["TPS61040DBVR", "LM27313XMF/NOPB", "LM2733XMF/NOPB"],
      "finding": "All three share the exact SOT-23-5 (DBV) pinout (1=SW, 2=GND, 3=FB, 4=EN/SHDN, 5=VIN) and ~1.23 V VREF, but differ sharply in voltage/current/Iq/compensation: TPS61040 caps VIN at 6 V (7 V abs max), 400 mA switch limit, PFM up to 1 MHz, 28 uA Iq; LM27313 extends VIN to 14 V, 800 mA min (1.25 A typ) switch, 30 V SW, 1.6 MHz PWM, 400 uA non-switching / 2.1 mA switching Iq, mandatory Cf across R1; LM2733X extends SW to 40 V and 1.0 A min (1.5 A typ) switch with mandatory Cf and higher 210 C/W RthetaJA."
    },
    {
      "group": "Ultra-Low-Iq Fixed 3.3 V Boost Converters (FB Strap & Disconnect Traps)",
      "parts": ["TPS613221ADBVR", "TPS61221DCKR", "TPS610994DRVR"],
      "finding": "Fixed 3.3 V FB wiring is opposite between TPS61221DCKR (Pin 2 FB MUST tie to VOUT) and TPS610994DRVR (Pin 3 FB MUST tie to GND). Shutdown disconnect also diverges: TPS613221ADBVR has no EN pin (always on), TPS61221DCKR allows body-diode pass-through when EN=0, while TPS610994DRVR provides true load disconnect plus down-mode regulation (and requires >= 400 us EN low pulse on toggle)."
    },
    {
      "group": "Legacy High-Voltage Non-Synchronous Bucks vs Modern Synchronous Bucks",
      "parts": ["TPS54331DR", "LM2596SX-5.0/NOPB"],
      "finding": "TPS54331DR uses standard non-PowerPAD SOIC-8 (D: RthetaJA 116.3 C/W vs 48.7 C/W on DDA), requires an external Schottky diode and COMP RC network, and limits EN to 6.0 V abs max. LM2596SX-5.0/NOPB (TO-263-5 with GND tab) has INVERTED active-low ON/OFF enable polarity (en_active_high: false), 150 kHz switching, 80% bipolar efficiency, 5 mA Iq, and requires bulky 33-47 uH inductors plus finite-ESR electrolytic/tantalum capacitors."
    }
